<refnamediv>
  <refname><type>SilikoFunction</type></refname>
  <refpurpose>Type providing an interface for an in-language
    function</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Function.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">typedef /* ... */ SilikoFunction;</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <type>SilikoFunction</type> type encapsulates an in-language
function for the Siliko language. Functions requiring a state object
can be built using a <type>SilikoFunctionVTable</type> with
<function>SilikoFunctionCreate</function> or a wrapper for a pure
function can be created with
<function>SilikoPureFunctionCreate</function>.</para>
</refsection>
